1
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:33,980
This is far enough.

2
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:39,770
Oh? You don't
need an escort, then?

3
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:42,989
I could do without one
who wants to kill me.

4
00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:44,110
You impress me.

5
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:49,370
It seems you know enough
to sense hostility, at least.

6
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:52,431
Rin has ordered me
to escort you peacefully,

7
00:00:52,443 --> 00:00:54,540
so I will refrain
from attacking you.

8
00:01:08,210 --> 00:01:13,250
In the face of absolute despair

9
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:17,250
That nearly burned
our hearts away

10
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:23,800
You still found the
courage to smile

11
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:28,600
Like you accepted it all

12
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,860
I lost my voice

13
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:34,480
And the things I wanted to say

14
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:39,730
But every time I
fell to my knees

15
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:44,030
I stood up and kept walking

16
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:49,700
We were looking for
the ideal white future

17
00:01:49,910 --> 00:01:54,930
Our one and only hope

18
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:57,420
Now I may be left with nothing

19
00:01:57,590 --> 00:02:02,840
But these raging
emotions that have

20
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,940
Nowhere to go

21
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:11,190
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

22
00:02:11,570 --> 00:02:14,600
With more than one right answer

23
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:18,430
I won't stop

24
00:02:18,730 --> 00:02:20,460
Until I find it

25
00:02:28,050 --> 00:02:29,169
Is that so?

26
00:02:29,170 --> 00:02:33,049
But if you want to go,
I'm happy to take you on.

27
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:36,519
I may be inexperienced,
but I am still a mage.

28
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,870
Don't be absurd.

29
00:02:37,871 --> 00:02:40,270
Mirage

30
00:02:40,271 --> 00:02:42,810
A mage who doesn't reek of
blood is worse than a novice.

31
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:46,189
You're saying that I don't
have the smell of blood on me?

32
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:50,989
Mages are beings who become cold-blooded
in order to achieve their goals.

33
00:02:50,990 --> 00:02:53,279
You should follow
Tohsaka Rin's example.

34
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:57,830
She might have a soft spot or two, but she
has the proper mindset, despite her age.

35
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:01,249
It's fortunate for you that
Tohsaka's your Master.

36
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:03,920
She's your best shot
at getting the Grail.

37
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:08,210
That malevolent treasure chest
that can grant human wishes?

38
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:10,670
I have no interest
in such a thing.

39
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:13,140
No interest?

40
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:16,778
Don't Servants fight in
this war to have a wish

41
00:03:16,790 --> 00:03:19,729
fulfilled that they
couldn't achieve in life?

42
00:03:19,730 --> 00:03:20,980
Hardly.

43
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,810
We're summoned with
no say in the matter.

44
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,190
We Servants have no free will.

45
00:03:27,690 --> 00:03:32,529
Your Saber is probably the only one
who answers the call of her own volition.

46
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:34,529
Only Saber?

47
00:03:34,530 --> 00:03:35,450
That's right.

48
00:03:35,451 --> 00:03:39,619
Heroic Spirits are called
forth by others' wills.

49
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:41,709
We're nothing more
than disposable tools.

50
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:48,460
Do you honestly believe that, in our
heart of hearts, we wish to help humans?

51
00:03:49,170 --> 00:03:50,590
Well...

52
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,259
Listen.

53
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:54,549
Heroic Spirits are
mere instruments...

54
00:03:54,550 --> 00:03:59,470
tools summoned to aid the disadvantaged and
disappear once their purpose is fulfilled.

55
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:05,100
They're sweepers, stripped of their
will and made to serve humans forever.

56
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:07,309
That is what Heroic Spirits are.

57
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:10,110
So-called "guardians" that are
summoned when it's convenient.

58
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:13,359
Instruments? What
are you talking about?

59
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,949
Saber is a person.

60
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:18,119
If she doesn't want to do
something, she refuses,

61
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:20,990
and I'm sure she can make her
own decisions now that she's here.

62
00:04:21,370 --> 00:04:22,539
Possibly.

63
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:25,488
Being provided with a
Servant's shell in itself

64
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:28,460
allows Heroic Spirits
to regain their humanity.

65
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:33,169
Along with old
obsessions and regrets.

66
00:04:33,170 --> 00:04:34,669
Regrets?

67
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:39,929
Put yourself in the shoes of those
who died with unfinished business,

68
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:44,310
only to find themselves brought
back by a human to do their bidding...

69
00:04:44,850 --> 00:04:49,059
all because they seek the Grail.

70
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:52,820
Then why aren't you interested
in something so powerful?

71
00:04:53,190 --> 00:04:56,280
I had no dream
that went unfulfilled.

72
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:01,450
I fulfilled my dream, died,
and became a Heroic Spirit.

73
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,870
So I have no wish
I want granted.

74
00:05:11,250 --> 00:05:12,420
I'm home.

75
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:15,049
Welcome back, Senpai.

76
00:05:15,050 --> 00:05:17,129
Hey. Welcome back, Shirou.

77
00:05:17,130 --> 00:05:19,850
Saber-chan was
really mad at you.

78
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:21,220
Yeah...

79
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:24,600
You know about Mitsuzuri-san?

80
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,480
They found her
a little while ago.

81
00:05:27,810 --> 00:05:30,059
They found Mitsuzuri?

82
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:32,519
Wait, how did you
know about that?

83
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:35,490
Ah, Ryuudou-kun
asked me to tell you.

84
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:38,449
He said her memory's
a bit jumbled,

85
00:05:38,450 --> 00:05:41,660
but there's no visible trauma and
her condition isn't life-threatening.

86
00:05:42,030 --> 00:05:44,329
Isn't that great news, Senpai?

87
00:05:44,330 --> 00:05:45,450
Yeah.

88
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,420
Sakura, do you have a minute?

89
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,760
It isn't safe after dark, so I want
you to spend the night here again.

90
00:05:58,340 --> 00:06:02,760
Actually, if possible, could you
keep staying here for a while?

91
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,770
Sorry. Am I putting
you on the spot?

92
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:09,139
Okay...

93
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:12,110
Um, I'll take you up
on your kind offer.

94
00:06:16,070 --> 00:06:17,070
Shirou.

95
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:20,740
You gave me your word that
you would return before sunset.

96
00:06:21,410 --> 00:06:22,819
I'm sorry.

97
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:25,449
You have every
right to be angry.

98
00:06:25,450 --> 00:06:29,750
But before you yell at me, do you
mind if we discuss our strategy first?

99
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:36,000
There was a third
Master at school.

100
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:41,930
So Tohsaka and I agreed to form
a truce until we can identify them.

101
00:06:43,930 --> 00:06:46,849
Are you opposed to
working with Tohsaka?

102
00:06:46,850 --> 00:06:47,929
No.

103
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:52,650
I merely wish you had consulted me
before making such an important decision.

104
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:56,109
Oh... Sorry.

105
00:06:56,110 --> 00:06:57,649
Just to be clear...

106
00:06:57,650 --> 00:07:00,183
After this Master at
your school is defeated,

107
00:07:00,195 --> 00:07:02,570
your truce with Rin
will be null and void.

108
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,740
Is that correct?

109
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:07,030
Yes.

110
00:07:07,370 --> 00:07:11,120
As long as you understand
that, I have no objection.

111
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:16,040
Let us work with Rin so that you
may gain more combat experience.

112
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:20,879
Saber, you need
the Grail, right?

113
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:21,760
Yes.

114
00:07:21,761 --> 00:07:24,300
But why do you need it?

115
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:29,430
Does this question have any
bearing on our future strategy?

116
00:07:29,930 --> 00:07:31,690
No, I just...

117
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:34,400
Did something happen, Shirou?

118
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:37,070
Forget it. It's nothing.

119
00:07:38,570 --> 00:07:40,650
I would like to
offer a suggestion.

120
00:07:42,150 --> 00:07:45,700
Moving forward, you should build
experience through hands-on training.

121
00:07:49,910 --> 00:07:51,750
Yeah, you're right.

122
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:54,750
Thanks in advance.

123
00:08:01,670 --> 00:08:03,010
Hey, Emiya!

124
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:06,509
Did you hear about Mitsuzuri?

125
00:08:06,510 --> 00:08:09,430
They told me at the
dojo just this morning.

126
00:08:09,890 --> 00:08:13,139
She was found in Shinto, huh?

127
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:14,979
In a back alley, no less.

128
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:18,940
I heard her eyes were glazed
over and her uniform was in tatters.

129
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:21,569
I don't know what happened,

130
00:08:21,570 --> 00:08:25,779
but how did a stuck-up girl like her
end up ditched in an alley like that?

131
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:28,489
As a friend, I can't help but...

132
00:08:28,490 --> 00:08:29,490
Shinji!

133
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:32,699
Wow, scary.

134
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,460
I'm just kidding.

135
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,960
It's only a rumor, right?

136
00:08:37,670 --> 00:08:42,590
But after yesterday, she's become
pretty infamous among the first-years.

137
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:45,630
You were the last person to
see Mitsuzuri, weren't you?

138
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:49,180
Yeah, but all we did
was make idle chitchat.

139
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:53,309
Don't jump to conclusions, now.

140
00:08:53,310 --> 00:08:57,980
If you throw around false
accusations, you'll regret it, Emiya.

141
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:10,450
You're asking how
to identify a Master?

142
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:14,620
If you were near a
Master, would you know?

143
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:19,499
I suppose, but only if they hadn't
made any attempt at hiding it.

144
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:24,550
A Master is a mage, so if you follow
their mana, you can locate them.

145
00:09:25,130 --> 00:09:27,469
But the most you'd
get is suspects.

146
00:09:27,470 --> 00:09:28,470
That's all.

147
00:09:30,390 --> 00:09:31,390
Emiya-kun?

148
00:09:33,180 --> 00:09:34,640
Trace on.

149
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:50,489
There really is one here.

150
00:09:50,490 --> 00:09:51,910
I'm impressed.

151
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:54,079
That's a sigil?

152
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:55,040
Yeah.

153
00:09:55,041 --> 00:09:58,539
Emiya-kun, for a guy who has no
sensitivity to living organisms' mana,

154
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:00,960
you're surprisingly good at
picking up local abnormalities.

155
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:07,090
Was that a compliment?

156
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:12,099
You didn't think I was a
mage either, remember?

157
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:14,060
Why was that?

158
00:10:14,510 --> 00:10:17,139
What? You want
me to spell it out?

159
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:18,480
No, forget it.

160
00:10:18,850 --> 00:10:20,729
I can guess.

161
00:10:20,730 --> 00:10:22,229
Clever boy.

162
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:24,189
Anyway, that's just how it is.

163
00:10:24,190 --> 00:10:30,109
Mages only recognize people with
a certain level of mana as mages.

164
00:10:30,110 --> 00:10:32,700
I thought it would be
something like that.

165
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:40,419
That should be most
of the active sigils.

166
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:43,629
You were able to disable
the magic field, then?

167
00:10:43,630 --> 00:10:48,169
The field itself is already in place,
so all I did was weaken its potency.

168
00:10:48,170 --> 00:10:50,589
Anyone who'd put
up a field like this

169
00:10:50,590 --> 00:10:53,429
isn't going to stand by
and let others interfere.

170
00:10:53,430 --> 00:10:57,430
I expect they'll show
themselves—maybe even tomorrow.

171
00:10:58,850 --> 00:11:00,730
You think so?

172
00:11:06,270 --> 00:11:07,270
Anyway,

173
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:10,490
I have other business to
see to, so I'm heading home.

174
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:14,120
I need to buy some
supplies for tomorrow.

175
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:17,659
You should head
home early today too.

176
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:21,000
What? Are you worried about me?

177
00:11:22,290 --> 00:11:24,169
Th-That's not it!

178
00:11:24,170 --> 00:11:26,039
We have an alliance now,

179
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:29,339
so if anything happens
to you, it'll spoil my plans.

180
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:32,510
That's all it was! I
just said it to be clear!

181
00:11:40,350 --> 00:11:45,520
Heading home so late after
all that tedious sigil-erasing?

182
00:11:47,270 --> 00:11:48,480
What did you say?

183
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:52,109
The magic field you've been
systematically dismantling

184
00:11:52,110 --> 00:11:54,989
is an insurance policy
I set up for myself.

185
00:11:54,990 --> 00:11:57,659
I knew it, Shinji. You're...

186
00:11:57,660 --> 00:12:00,499
Please don't be so stiff, Emiya.

187
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:05,170
Just like you, I don't have any
mana, but they're making me a Master.

188
00:12:05,670 --> 00:12:07,749
So what's the
story with that field?

189
00:12:07,750 --> 00:12:11,009
I told you, it's just insurance.

190
00:12:11,010 --> 00:12:13,510
Then are you the one who
attacked that student yesterday?

191
00:12:14,380 --> 00:12:17,139
I didn't have any choice there.

192
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:19,640
My Servant did it on her own.

193
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,979
Come on, you have to believe me.

194
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:25,770
I don't want to fight anyone.

195
00:12:26,690 --> 00:12:27,980
All right.

196
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,520
Wait, Emiya!

197
00:12:30,110 --> 00:12:32,070
Will you team up with me?

198
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:36,279
My family, the Matous,
was once a lineage of mages.

199
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,619
The Matous?

200
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:42,539
Well, it's no surprise that you wouldn't
know, since you aren't a proper mage.

201
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:45,290
If you don't believe
me, ask Tohsaka.

202
00:12:45,790 --> 00:12:49,710
Shinji, does Sakura
know about you?

203
00:12:50,170 --> 00:12:53,720
Mage families only pass down
their secret arts to the eldest son.

204
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:57,510
As if anyone would teach
magic to that dunce of a girl.

205
00:12:58,140 --> 00:12:59,850
Well? What do you say?

206
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:04,730
If you aren't going to do anything,
what's the point of working together?

207
00:13:07,690 --> 00:13:10,149
So teaming up's a no-go, huh?

208
00:13:10,150 --> 00:13:15,240
Emiya, don't tell me
you're actually in this to win.

209
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:19,239
I see.

210
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:21,759
Well, I can hardly leave
my sister in the home of

211
00:13:21,771 --> 00:13:24,199
one who's taking part
in this slaughter, can I?

212
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,659
Fine.

213
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:27,960
I'll tell Sakura myself.

214
00:13:28,330 --> 00:13:32,340
Okay. I'm glad you care for
her so much as her senior.

215
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:36,259
What we discussed here is
just between you and me, right?

216
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:40,550
I came clean out of
respect for our friendship.

217
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:43,180
Sure, I'll keep quiet.

218
00:13:52,150 --> 00:13:53,150
You're wide open!

219
00:14:05,830 --> 00:14:07,830
Okay, one more match!

220
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,329
Ouch...

221
00:14:11,330 --> 00:14:13,000
Damn Saber.

222
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:16,090
When she decides to do
something, she doesn't hold back.

223
00:14:20,470 --> 00:14:22,050
Trace on.

224
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,900
Crap. Concentrate!

225
00:14:34,110 --> 00:14:35,110
Shirou?

226
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:38,069
What is it, Saber?

227
00:14:38,070 --> 00:14:41,110
Nothing. I just sensed magic.

228
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:42,949
You are training?

229
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:46,870
Yeah. I do this every day.

230
00:14:47,370 --> 00:14:49,120
May I enter?

231
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:51,000
Sure.

232
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:55,339
I heard that your magical
specialty is fortification.

233
00:14:55,340 --> 00:15:00,009
It's the only thing I can do, so I'm
not sure if "specialty" is the word.

234
00:15:00,010 --> 00:15:03,510
How does one train in
the art of fortification?

235
00:15:04,050 --> 00:15:08,599
Fortification isn't just about
increasing a thing's toughness.

236
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:11,440
It also includes
increasing its effectiveness.

237
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,900
For this rock, it's
making it harder.

238
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:17,440
For that light bulb,
it's making it brighter.

239
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:20,359
I visualize an
object's components

240
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:24,910
and pass my mana
through them to fortify it.

241
00:15:25,450 --> 00:15:26,530
I understand.

242
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:31,040
I-It's better to show than tell.

243
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:34,250
I'll try it on this.

244
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:36,170
Trace on.

245
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:42,260
Tracing fundamental structure.

246
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:45,090
Tracing auxiliary components.

247
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:48,100
Altering fundamental structure.

248
00:15:48,810 --> 00:15:52,480
Reinforcing
auxiliary components.

249
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:57,360
Damn, another bust.

250
00:15:58,070 --> 00:16:00,989
My success rate is
actually pretty low.

251
00:16:00,990 --> 00:16:06,870
No, I sensed just now that
your concentration was lacking.

252
00:16:07,580 --> 00:16:08,450
Oh...

253
00:16:08,451 --> 00:16:14,330
No, my luck is a lot better
with bladed tools like this.

254
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:18,920
I can see that my presence
here is a distraction.

255
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:21,550
Please try not to
push yourself too hard.

256
00:16:22,670 --> 00:16:24,970
I won't. Goodnight.

257
00:17:12,930 --> 00:17:14,100
Is this...

258
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:16,599
Ryuudou Temple?

259
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,350
Yes, it is.

260
00:17:33,950 --> 00:17:36,080
Mmm... Roasted cod roe...

261
00:17:45,010 --> 00:17:46,260
Shirou.

262
00:17:52,390 --> 00:17:54,639
The Caster-class Servant?

263
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:58,310
Indeed I am, Master of Saber.

264
00:17:59,690 --> 00:18:01,059
Do not bother.

265
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:05,939
Once cast, a spell cannot be
washed away with the water of mana.

266
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:10,160
Especially not by the flow from
magic circuits as feeble as yours.

267
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:12,989
Meaning that I was
easy to summon here?

268
00:18:12,990 --> 00:18:17,709
Because, of all the Masters,
you are the weakest by far.

269
00:18:17,710 --> 00:18:19,999
You're going to kill me?

270
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:24,669
Rest easy. If I killed you, I wouldn't
be able to drain you of mana.

271
00:18:24,670 --> 00:18:28,089
I did inadvertently kill a few
before I had the feel for it,

272
00:18:28,090 --> 00:18:30,430
but now, I can collect
just the right amount.

273
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:33,929
You're the one behind
the people fainting in town?

274
00:18:33,930 --> 00:18:36,180
Oh, you didn't know?

275
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:40,440
We Servants of the Caster class have
the prerogative of establishing territory.

276
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:45,229
By building a sanctuary here,
I've protected myself from you.

277
00:18:45,230 --> 00:18:46,940
You can see it, can't you?

278
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:51,159
The mana of hundreds of
people stored in this soil...

279
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:53,200
The fragments of the rabble.

280
00:18:53,530 --> 00:18:58,949
Caster... You
involved outsiders?

281
00:18:58,950 --> 00:19:02,169
All the people in this
town belong to me.

282
00:19:02,170 --> 00:19:03,919
Caster!

283
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:07,669
Well, I think we have
talked for long enough.

284
00:19:07,670 --> 00:19:10,840
Let's get those
Command Spells off you.

285
00:19:22,190 --> 00:19:25,650
A magic field that repels the
very concept of Heroic Spirits?

286
00:19:36,530 --> 00:19:37,530
If I may:

287
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:39,700
what class of Servant are you?

288
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:42,079
The Assassin-class Servant,

289
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:44,210
Sasaki Kojirou.

290
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:48,959
Isn't it natural to identify
oneself before combat?

291
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,906
If my opponent should
identify themselves,

292
00:19:50,918 --> 00:19:52,970
I am honor-bound as
a knight to do the same.

293
00:19:53,510 --> 00:19:56,259
Once I have done so, I
will make you step aside.

294
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:58,100
My name is...

295
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:58,100
It matters not.

296
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:04,650
My blade will tell me all I
need to know of my enemy.

297
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:10,229
If you wish to pass, then
force your way through.

298
00:20:10,230 --> 00:20:13,569
You want to take
my Command Spells?

299
00:20:13,570 --> 00:20:14,570
That's right.

300
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:18,329
I will transplant them
onto my own Master.

301
00:20:18,330 --> 00:20:23,210
And then, he will have Saber deal
with that troublesome Berserker.

302
00:20:23,710 --> 00:20:30,170
Removing Command Spells also
requires extracting your magic circuits.

303
00:20:40,770 --> 00:20:42,889
That's a good boy.

304
00:20:42,890 --> 00:20:46,060
I do enjoy it when you struggle.

305
00:20:58,740 --> 00:21:01,039
I expected to find
you long dead,

306
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:03,120
but it seems you're more
tenacious than I'd thought.

307
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:05,330
You...

308
00:21:05,660 --> 00:21:06,670
Why?

309
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:14,170
Oh, I merely happened by.

310
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:17,090
So, are you able to move now?

311
00:21:17,550 --> 00:21:20,390
My arrows should have
severed Caster's threads.

312
00:21:21,930 --> 00:21:24,059
Yeah, I can.

313
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:25,559
Good to hear.

314
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:29,559
As much as I would like
to say, "Do what you want,"

315
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,940
I suggest you stay
where you are for now.

316
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:34,690
If you act without thinking...

317
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:37,110
You are Archer?

318
00:21:38,450 --> 00:21:40,869
Damn that Assassin!
What is he doing?

319
00:21:40,870 --> 00:21:45,330
See? She'll take
her anger out on you.

320
00:21:45,660 --> 00:21:48,960
A woman's fury is
difficult to control.

321
00:21:49,790 --> 00:21:51,249
Damn.

322
00:21:51,250 --> 00:21:54,260
I think things are
about to get a bit violent.

323
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:16,499
We didn't understand anything

324
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:22,669
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

325
00:22:22,670 --> 00:22:25,669
A moral conflict

326
00:22:25,670 --> 00:22:28,470
stays your hand

327
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:31,219
and tricks you

328
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:33,100
out of your future

329
00:22:33,350 --> 00:22:40,019
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

330
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:45,820
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

331
00:22:46,030 --> 00:22:54,030
but I want to live my life

332
00:22:55,030 --> 00:23:00,039
The past repeats before my eyes

333
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:07,839
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

334
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:13,929
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

335
00:23:13,930 --> 00:23:19,559
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

336
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:23,270
Fight your fate

337
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:28,559
I wouldn't want your
help, even if you offered!

338
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:30,559
If you're both an idiot and
a child, you're a lost cause.

339
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:34,189
I shall mete out an appropriate punishment
upon those who would call me a witch.

340
00:23:34,190 --> 00:23:36,730
A Servant who created a technique
on par with a Noble Phantasm...

341
00:23:36,731 --> 00:23:38,735
The Reward for the Death Match

342
00:23:38,736 --> 00:23:40,990
Next Time

343
00:23:36,730 --> 00:23:40,110
Shall I break open that
belief with brute force?

